  (W, "The default address type is the kind of address that a wallet gives out when the user does not ask for another. In Bitcoin Core it is controlled by the option addresstype, whose help text lists the possible values as legacy, p2sh-segwit, bech32 and bech32m, with the default bech32 [CORE]. The command getnewaddress accepts the same four values as its address type argument, and its default is whatever the option sets [CORE]."),
