  (W, "Exporting a single key means taking one private key out of a wallet, usually as a wallet import format string, so that it can be put into another wallet. It was an everyday operation of the early wallets, which held independent keys, and Bitcoin Core offered the commands dumpprivkey to export a key and importprivkey to import one. The book says that almost no modern wallets support the ability to export or import an individual key [BK]."),
